              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imitor, imitārī — \"to imitate, to copy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fīlius patrem imitātur. The son imitates his father."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: imitor, imitārī, imitātus sum, with the accusative. English imitate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of imitor is not settled; Lewis & Short give no sure account, though it is often grouped with the word for an image. English imitate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
